MigrateIntegrationConcreteTest
├── When the new locker factory is not set
│   └── It should revert with {MigrationDisabled}
└── When the new locker factory is set
    ├── When the locker does not exist
    │   └── It should revert with {NotLocker}
    └── When the locker exists
        ├── When the caller is the pool launcher
        │   ├── When the amounts to unlock are smaller than the amounts to migrate
        │   │   └── It should revert with {InsufficientUnlockMin}
        │   └── When the amounts to unlock are greater than or equal to the amounts to migrate
        │       ├── When the amounts unlocked are smaller than the min amounts to unlock
        │       │   └── It should revert with {PS}
        │       └── When the amounts unlocked are greater than or equal to the min amounts to unlock
        │           ├── It should remove the old locker instance from the factory
        │           ├── It should update the liquidity for the underlying pool
        │           ├── It should update the lock count for the underlying pool
        │           ├── It should unlock the old locker and withdraw all liquidity to the pool launcher
        │           ├── It should burn the old liquidity position
        │           ├── It should return the unlocked token amounts
        │           └── It should emit a {LockerUnlocked} event
        └── When the caller is not the pool launcher
            ├── When the caller is not the owner
            │   └── It should revert with {NotLockerOwnerOrPoolLauncher}
            └── When the caller is the owner
                ├── When the locker is not locked
                │   └── It should revert with {NotLocked}
                └── When the locker is locked
                    ├── When the amounts to unlock are smaller than the amounts to migrate_
                    │   └── It should revert with {InsufficientUnlockMin}
                    └── When the amounts to unlock are greater than or equal to the amounts to migrate_
                        ├── When the amounts unlocked are smaller than the min amounts to unlock_
                        │   └── It should revert with {PS}
                        └── When the amounts unlocked are greater than or equal to the min amounts to unlock_
                            ├── When the amounts migrated are smaller than the min amounts
                            │   └── It should revert with {PSC}
                            └── When the amounts migrated are greater than or equal to the min amounts
                                ├── It should remove the old locker instance from the factory
                                ├── It should update the liquidity for the underlying pool
                                ├── It should update the lock count for the underlying pool
                                ├── It should unlock the old locker and withdraw all liquidity
                                ├── It should burn the old liquidity position
                                ├── It should mint a liquidity position on the new deployment
                                ├── It should refund any leftover tokens to the new locker
                                ├── It should reset any outstanding allowances
                                ├── It should lock the LP in an identical locker in the new factory
                                ├── It should return the unlocked token amounts
                                ├── It should emit a {LockerUnlocked} event
                                └── It should emit a {LockerMigrated} event
